@@name
fix-defect
@@description
Fix the defect described in the user request so the code behaves as the user expects, without changing unrelated behaviour.
@@requirements
    - Reproduce the defect first (failing test, command, or minimal script) and record the exact failure
    - Fix the root cause, not the symptom; name the cause in your report
    - Add or update a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after it
@@approach
    Before editing, reason through:
    - Where the incorrect behaviour originates, traced from the reproduction rather than guessed
    - Whether other callers depend on the current (buggy) behaviour
    Select the smallest fix that removes the cause and commit to it.
@@verification
    - Re-run the reproduction and confirm the defect no longer occurs
@@constraints
    - Keep the change minimal: no drive-by refactors or formatting changes in touched files
    - Do not weaken, skip or delete existing tests to make them pass
@@out-of-scope
    - Unrelated bugs you notice (list them in the report instead of fixing them)
